  "description": "Microsoft's security updates (2026-Oct, 2026-Sep) fix 1311 CVEs for Windows Server 2016, Windows 10 Version 1607 (build 10.0.14393); the newest fix is 10.0.14393.9612, an older version is affected by at least one of them. Most severe: CVE-2026-100202 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-100215 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-100220 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-102211 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-102214 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-102225 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-108131 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-108399 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-108460 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-108467 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9612), CVE-2026-69499 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9512), CVE-2026-69518 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9512), CVE-2026-69579 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9512), CVE-2026-69590 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9512), CVE-2026-69595 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9512), CVE-2026-69601 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9512), CVE-2026-69603 (fixed in 10.0.14393.9512) and 63 more",
